### TimeEntry API: every route, against the API itself (spec item E04).
###
### Run the API (dotnet run --project TimeEntry.ApiService, or the Aspire AppHost) and set @host to the address it listens on.
### The API serves routes WITHOUT "/api": the "/api" prefix belongs to the UI's proxy, which strips it before it reaches here.
### Every request but the sign-in needs the token from the first request. Put your own user name and password below
### (never commit them); on an empty database the first user is the one in the Bootstrap settings (see the README).

@host = http://localhost:5084
@userName = your-user-name
@password = your-password

### Sign in: the token is used by every request below
# @name login
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userName": "{{userName}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- reference data (everyone reads; Admin and Human Resources write)

### Departments (with their teams)
GET {{host}}/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/departments/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A department is found by name (an empty list when none match)
GET {{host}}/departments/Engineering
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add: a name of letters, digits, spaces, apostrophes and hyphens; 422 when an active department has it
POST {{host}}/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "departmentId": 0, "name": "Example Department", "isActive": true, "isDefault": false }

### Change: the teams in the body are changed, added or removed with it; leave "teams" out to leave them alone
PUT {{host}}/departments/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "departmentId": 1, "name": "Example Department", "isActive": true, "isDefault": false }

### Delete: 200, 404 when there is none, 400 when something uses it
DELETE {{host}}/departments/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Teams of one department
GET {{host}}/departmentteams/department/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/departmentteams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "departmentTeamId": 0, "departmentId": 1, "name": "Example Team", "isActive": true, "isDefault": false }

### Employees (with manager, department and team)
GET {{host}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Just the id and name of the active employees, for drop-downs
GET {{host}}/employees/lookup
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/employees/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Holidays: two may share a name
GET {{host}}/holidays
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/holidays
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "holidayId": 0, "sY_IsoCountry_Alpha3Code": "USA", "date": "2026-12-25T00:00:00", "name": "Example Holiday" }

### Projects (with their tasks) and the tasks
GET {{host}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "projectId": 0, "name": "Example Project", "isActive": true, "isDefault": false }

###
GET {{host}}/projecttasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The tasks of one project
GET {{host}}/projecttasks/project/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Periods in which leave may not be taken
GET {{host}}/restrictleaves
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- an employee's own rows (each caller sees their own, their reports', or all as Admin / HR)
### The big lists take ?pageIndex=0&pageSize=25&sort=column:desc&search=text and then answer { pageIndex, pageSize, count, data };
### without a page parameter they answer the whole list as an array. A bad page, size or sort column is a 400 that names the choices.

### Time sheets: newest first
GET {{host}}/timesheets?pageIndex=0&pageSize=10&sort=whenEntered:desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/timesheets?pageIndex=0&pageSize=10&sort=employee:asc&search=smith
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The owner is the signed-in employee, whoever the body names (Admin and HR may name anyone)
POST {{host}}/timesheets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "timeSheetId": 0, "employeeId": 1, "whenEntered": "2026-10-05T00:00:00", "notes": "example" }

### The details of one time sheet, with project and task names
GET {{host}}/timesheetDetails/timeSheet/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/timesheetDetails
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "timeSheetDetailId": 0, "e_TimeSheetId": 1, "projectId": 1, "projectTaskId": 1,
  "sundayHours": 0, "mondayHours": 8, "tuesdayHours": 0, "wednesdayHours": 0, "thursdayHours": 0, "fridayHours": 0, "saturdayHours": 0, "notes": "" }

### Requests (the server sets when it was requested; nobody approves their own)
GET {{host}}/requests?pageIndex=0&pageSize=10&sort=whenRequested:desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestId": 0, "employeeId": 1, "sY_RequestStatusTypeId": 0, "overtimeTypeId": 1, "overtimeHrsRequested": 2, "reason": "example overtime" }

### Leave donations
GET {{host}}/donateleaves?pageIndex=0&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Expense sheets (with their details) and the details
GET {{host}}/expenseSheets?pageIndex=0&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/expenseSheets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestExpenseSheetId": 0, "projectId": 1, "employeeId": 1, "notes": "example" }

###
GET {{host}}/expenseDetails?pageIndex=0&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Responses to requests (managers, HR and Admin write)
GET {{host}}/responses?pageIndex=0&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- users (Admin only; a password or answer is never shown)
GET {{host}}/timeentryusers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
